.TH VIZ 1 "September 2026" "0.1.0-rc.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
viz \- compile project evidence into reproducible terminal demonstrations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B viz
.I COMMAND
.RI [ PATH ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B viz
inspects a project, explains the facts it detects, ranks the commands that
would best demonstrate the project, and writes a deterministic VHS tape
recording them.
.PP
The safety boundary is explicit:
.B inspect
and
.B generate
only read project files and never execute project code;
.B render
is the only command that executes a tape, through the external VHS renderer.
Always review generated commands before rendering.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI viz inspect " [ PATH ] [ \-\-json ]"
Explain the detected project facts (with source file and line) and the ranked
demonstration commands. With
.BR \-\-json ,
prints the project, evidence, and commands as JSON. Default path: the current
directory.
.TP
.BR viz generate " | " init " | " new " [ " PATH " ] [ OPTIONS ]"
Write a deterministic VHS tape for the project (default output:
.IR <project>/demo.tape ).
.B init
and
.B new
are aliases of
.BR generate .
.TP
.BI viz check " <TAPE>"
Validate the tape structure and parse it with the external VHS tool. Requires
.B vhs
on PATH.
.TP
.BI viz render " <TAPE> [ \-o " MEDIA ]
Validate the tape, then explicitly execute it through the external VHS
renderer. Requires
.B vhs
on PATH. With
.IR \-o ,
VHS writes GIF, MP4, or WebM media to
.IR MEDIA .
.TP
.BR viz " " help | \-h | \-\-help
Print the help text.
.TP
.BR viz " " version | \-V | \-\-version
Print the version.
.SS "generate options"
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " <TAPE>"
Tape path (default:
.IR <project>/demo.tape ).
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-stdout .
.TP
.BI \-\-media " <PATH>"
GIF, MP4, or WebM output embedded in the tape.
.TP
.BI \-\-command " <SHELL>"
Record this command instead of an inferred command; repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Include every inferred command.
.TP
.BI \-\-title " <TEXT>"
Override the displayed project title.
.TP
.BI \-\-width " <PX>"
Terminal width. (default: 1200)
.TP
.BI \-\-height " <PX>"
Terminal height. (default: 720)
.TP
.BI \-\-font\-size " <PX>"
Font size from 8 to 72. (default: 18)
.TP
.BI \-\-typing\-speed " <MS>"
Delay per typed character. (default: 35)
.TP
.B \-\-stdout
Print the tape instead of writing it. Cannot be combined with
.B \-\-output
or
.BR \-\-force .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Replace an existing tape atomically.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Inspection, filesystem, or external VHS failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown command or option, missing tape argument, conflicting
output modes).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I demo.tape
Default tape written by
.BR "viz generate" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B vhs
The external VHS executable must be on PATH for
.B check
and
.BR render .
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect a project and list ranked demo commands:
.RS 4
.B viz inspect ~/src/myapp
.RE
.PP
Generate a tape with custom media and title:
.RS 4
.B viz generate \-\-media out.gif \-\-title "My App" \-\-output demo.tape
.RE
.PP
Validate, then render:
.RS 4
.B viz check demo.tape
.B viz render demo.tape \-o demo.gif
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
The README at https://github.com/elci-group/viz and the VHS tape format
documentation at https://github.com/charmbracelet/vhs .
.SH BUGS
Report bugs on the GitHub issue tracker at
https://github.com/elci-group/viz/issues
